#====================================================================
# E235 — Select an OHOS-compatible OpenSSL entropy source
#====================================================================

id:                     E235
trigger_tool:           openssl|clang|lld|conan
phase:                  compilation|linking|testing
error_signature:        undefined symbol: __fd_chk|libdefault-lib-rand_unix.o.*__fd_chk|rand_unix.c.*__fd_chk

severity:               3
category:               crypto|openssl|ohos-sdk|entropy
match_keywords:         OpenSSL, OHOS, __fd_chk, rand_unix.c, RAND_bytes, FD_SET, DEVRANDOM_WAIT, getrandom, libcrypto.a
title:                  Select an OHOS-compatible OpenSSL entropy source

root_cause:             OpenSSL's default OS random seeding enables both getrandom and a DEVRANDOM_WAIT fallback.
                        The fallback compiles FD_SET in rand_unix.c; the OHOS SDK lowers that operation to the
                        private fortified helper __fd_chk, but the target SDK libraries do not export the helper.
                        A shallow consumer that never calls RAND_bytes can leave rand_unix.o unlinked and miss the defect.
affected_scope:         OpenSSL 3.x static archives cross-built for OHOS with a Linux-family Configure target,
                        especially when they are later linked into shared downstream libraries.
verification_cmd:       llvm-nm -u libcrypto.a | rg __fd_chk; link and run a real RAND_bytes consumer; run openssl version -a

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           select-supported-getrandom-seed
rec_description:        Configure OpenSSL with --with-rand-seed=getrandom so the supported kernel entropy syscall
                        remains enabled while the unsupported DEVRANDOM_WAIT and FD_SET fallback is excluded.
                        Verify the result through a RAND_bytes consumer.
rec_command:            perl ./Configure linux-aarch64 --with-rand-seed=getrandom no-asm no-shared -fPIC; make build_sw build_tests
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-recipe

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      dedicated-ohos-random-port
fallback_description:   If a target does not support getrandom, implement and upstream an audited OHOS entropy
                        backend using a documented public system API, then exercise it with RAND_bytes and upstream RAND tests.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          source-port

forbid_1_pattern:       __fd_chk.*shim|stub.*__fd_chk
forbid_1_reason:        A private compatibility shim guesses SDK fortify semantics and hides an invalid static archive dependency at a cryptographic boundary.
forbid_1_consequence:   Downstream links may succeed while descriptor validation or entropy acquisition is incorrect.

forbid_2_pattern:       --with-rand-seed=none
forbid_2_reason:        Disabling automatic random seeding breaks key generation and other cryptographic operations.
forbid_2_consequence:   RAND-dependent APIs fail or operate without valid entropy.

principles:             P010, P012

causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E006]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

doc_file:               doc/E235.md
last_updated:           2026-07-25
source_event:           curl 8.15.0 and OpenSSL 3.5.6.1 HarmonyOS PC adaptation

authors:                2301_79503900 <3308319887@qq.com>
source_pr:              3047
source_commit:          eee475f7583efbd2f74ff4806fe90e5e07486374

metrics_success_count:  2
metrics_fail_count:     1
metrics_confidence:     0.90
